<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Saint Kitts and Nevis</h1><p class="st-meta">1983 CE – present · capital Basseterre</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The smallest sovereign state in the Americas, a two-island federation independent since 1983 whose constitution allows Nevis to secede.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anguilla">Anguilla's</a> separation, the remaining part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-christopher-nevis-anguilla">Saint Christopher-Nevis-Anguilla</a> became independent on 19 September 1983 as the Federation of Saint Christopher and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nevis">Nevis</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kennedy-simmonds">Kennedy Simmonds</a> as prime minister and the British monarch as head of state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution gave <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nevis">Nevis</a> its own island assembly and the right to secede by a two-thirds vote; a referendum in 1998 produced a majority for separation but fell short of the threshold. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denzil-douglas">Denzil Douglas</a> of the Labour Party governed from 1995 to 2015. The state-owned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> industry, the islands' economic mainstay for over three centuries, was closed in 2005, and tourism and the citizenship by investment programme, begun in 1984, became the main sources of revenue.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The federation remains a parliamentary democracy within the Commonwealth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terrance-drew">Terrance Drew</a> became prime minister in 2022. Relations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nevis">Nevis</a>, and dependence on passport sales, continue to shape its politics.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saint-kitts-and-nevis.jpg" alt="Saint Kitts and Nevis" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Edrice Lewis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saint_Kitts_and_Nevis.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1983 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Basseterre</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kennedy Simmonds, Denzil Douglas, Terrance Drew</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism and Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saint-kitts-and-nevis">Saint Kitts and Nevis</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federation of Saint Christopher and Nevis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2004&amp;focus=saint-kitts-and-nevis" aria-label="Saint Kitts and Nevis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2975 1535 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Saint Kitts and Nevis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3295 1791L3295 1791"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3295 1791h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Basseterre. <a href="/atlas?year=2004&amp;focus=saint-kitts-and-nevis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
